# Agent implementation guard (Steve)

## 99% certainty before code

Do **not** implement a feature unless you are **≥99% sure** you understand:

- What Steve asked for (not what a prior agent assumed)
- Where it lives in the UI today
- Whether it replaces, extends, or duplicates existing behavior

If ambiguous: **ask one short clarifying question** or propose **two options in plain language** and wait. Do not “helpfully” ship a parallel UI path.

## Architecture changes — discuss first

Stop and discuss with Steve **before coding** when the change would:

- Add or remove **tabs**, **panels**, **docks**, or **entry points** to the same workflow
- Split one surface into two (e.g. chat in sidebar **and** scene dock)
- Move state between sidebar ↔ scene ↔ full-page modes
- Change default navigation (Welcome → Briefing → Play → Differential)
- Introduce a new data path (localStorage shape, API route, case JSON field) used across modes

**Allowed without a design chat:** bug fixes, copy, synonyms, CSS within an existing surface, prompt/cache tweaks that do not add UI chrome.

## Play mode — canonical chrome (do not regress)

Steve wants **one** order/chat surface on the scene, not duplicate tabs.

| Surface | Role | Canonical? |
|---------|------|------------|
| **`SceneOrderCommandDock`** (scene, left) | Orders + chat input; **conversation expands here** (message icon) | **Yes — chat home** |
| **Floating sidebar** (`CaseContextPanel`) | HPI · Physical exam · **Orders stacks** · **Results** only | Yes — clinical context |
| ~~Sidebar **Thread** tab~~ | Was `showChatTab` + `chatPanel` in `Play.jsx` | **Removed** — do not re-add without Steve |
| **Differential Practice** | Separate full-page study mode; own floating chat | Different mode — not Play |

**Where “extra tabs” came from:** `CaseContextPanel.jsx` defines `CASE_TAB_DEFS` (HPI, exam, orders, results, **Thread**). Play used to set `showChatTab` and mount `PlayChatNotesTabPanel` in the sidebar while also showing quick-reply in the dock — **two chat UIs**. That duplication was agent-driven, not a Steve spec. Current rule: **dock only** for Play conversation.

## Before adding UI

1. Name the **single** surface Steve will use.
2. Say what you will **not** add (e.g. “no new sidebar tab”).
3. If unsure, link to this rule and ask.
